Task 1:Plan the Agent
Every point of the warehouse will be represented by coordinates (r,c) which represent the respective
row and column respectively.Hence every state as well the warehouse will be represented.The transition function determines the next state based on the selected action. An action is valid if the resulting cell is within the grid boundaries and does not contain an obstacle.The goal will be will have its unique coordinates which will be equal to the state S when reached.The frontier stores the unexpanded states that have been discovered by the agent. Each state contains its current grid position, its parent state, and the action used to reach it. A separate visited set is maintained to prevent repeated exploration of the same state.When the goal state is reached, the final path is reconstructed using the parent information stored during the search. Starting from the goal state, the agent repeatedly follows the parent of the current state until it reaches the initial state. The resulting sequence is then reversed to obtain the path.

